    {
      "attributes": {
        "description": "Milestone 6.3 (id 29): 'ciamUnknown (question, owner, blocking, answer) included in the planner verdict.' Started 2026-10-15 at the user's request to keep idle workers busy. Design first, escalate (kind decision) with your recommendation before building: where unknowns live (container, which domain owns them: likely governance or the planner's own), attributes (question, owner party, blocking yes/no, answer, answered-on, the environment(s)/entries it concerns, raised-on/due), how the planner verdict counts them (an open blocking unknown = a blocker? an open non-blocking one = an action? answered ones = info), report(s) (`opsdir report unknowns`), governed writes like any entry, docs. Reuse existing patterns (findings, keepers/owner parties, due dates from lead times) before adding new ones. RESERVED NUMBERS (another worker may add schema in parallel): core attributes 661-669, object classes 137-139; use only these. Showcase: propose whether to plant an unknown (it would change golden: plan and reports); the master re-baselines golden when the diff is what you predicted. Find the right flow(s) (planner verdict, governance) and set task/file flow_ids accordingly; add a flow if none fits. Rules 2991 (+ 3002's line-length/AIMFP rules). Boundary: the core domain you choose for unknowns, the planner verdict code, schema LDIF regeneration (opsdir/schema via gen-schema.py), docs, showcase data (examples/showcase/example_estate, data via gen-synthetic.py) if planting is approved, their tests. Not: cloud adapters, kits, format packages, core environment.py.",
